2026-04-21 04:01:31,875[utu.hooks.base_hooks] - DEBUG - base_hooks.py:41 - [toolcall-chatcmpl-tool-9c35ab115355f176] execute_python_code({"code": "def find_units_digit_of_product():\n    # Units digits of the even numbers we consider\n    units_digits = [2, 4, 6, 8]\n\n    # Calculate the units digit of the product of these units digits\n    units_digit_product = 1\n    for digit in units_digits:\n        units_digit_product *= digit\n        units_digit_product %= 10  # Keep only the units digit\n\n    # Since we are excluding numbers ending in 0, we need to consider the full set of even numbers\n    # and how their units digits interact. We can use the fact that the units digit of a product\n    # cycles through a pattern.\n    # For simplicity, let's calculate the units digit of the product of the first few sets of these numbers\n    # and see if we can identify a pattern.\n    \n    # Calculate the units digit of the product of the first few sets of these numbers\n    units_digit_product_full = 1\n    for i in range(1, 50):  # Considering the first 50 even numbers (to cover the range 2 to 98)\n        units_digit_product_full *= units_digits[i % 4]  # Use the pattern of 2, 4, 6, 8\n        units_digit_product_full %= 10  # Keep only the units digit\n    \n    return units_digit_product_full\n\nunits_digit = find_units_digit_of_product()", "timeout": 30}) - MainThread
